# Consumer-owned schema extension (issue 07 — Projects & Tasks core). The
# generated createTask / createTaskDependency CRUD mutations remain as low-level
# primitives, but each exposes a server-owned concern a client must never set:
#
#   * createTask trusts a client-supplied reporterID — provenance the server
#     must own (PRD story 30). createTaskInProject sets the Reporter to the
#     authenticated caller and lets tenant scoping inject the Workspace, so a
#     client controls only the work item's own fields.
#   * createTaskDependency cannot set the two junction FKs at all — the generated
#     GraphQL input omits the composite-PK task references, so the raw mutation
#     can never link two Tasks. addTaskDependency is the blessed surface that
#     names both Tasks and, because task_dependencies carries no workspace_id,
#     guards tenant isolation itself by requiring both Tasks to be visible in the
#     Active Workspace before writing.
#
# This mirrors how bootstrapWorkspace (issue 03) and inviteToWorkspace (issue 04)
# are preferred over their raw generated counterparts. Resolver bodies live in
# task_core.resolvers.go and are preserved across `sqlgen generate` by gqlgen's
# copy-through semantics.

"""
Details for creating a Task in a Project. The Reporter is not part of the input:
it is set server-side to the authenticated caller (PRD story 30), and the owning
Workspace is injected from the Active Workspace by tenant scoping — a client
controls only the work item's own fields.
"""
input CreateTaskInProjectInput {
  "Project the Task belongs to; must live in the Active Workspace"
  projectID: UUID!
  "Parent Task for a Subtask; omit for a top-level Task (PRD story 22)"
  parentTaskID: UUID
  "Short task summary"
  title: String!
  "Optional long-form description"
  description: String
  "Initial lifecycle state; defaults to BACKLOG when omitted"
  status: TaskStatus
  "Relative urgency; defaults to MEDIUM when omitted"
  priority: TaskPriority
}

extend type Mutation {
  """
  Create a Task in a Project within the Active Workspace, recording the
  authenticated caller as its Reporter (PRD stories 21, 30; and 22 when a
  parentTaskID nests it as a Subtask). Pass
  parentTaskID to create a Subtask under an existing Task. Unlike the generated
  createTask, the Reporter and owning Workspace are server-owned, never
  client-supplied.
  """
  createTaskInProject(input: CreateTaskInProjectInput!): Task!

  """
  Declare that one Task depends on another within the Active Workspace (PRD
  story 23). Both Tasks must be visible in the Active Workspace — the
  task_dependencies junction carries no workspace_id, so this mutation enforces
  tenant isolation by resolving both Tasks through tenant scoping first. Once
  written, the link is readable from either side: Task.dependsOnTasks lists a
  Task's dependencies and Task.tasks lists its dependents (story 24). type
  defaults to BLOCKS when omitted.
  """
  addTaskDependency(taskID: UUID!, dependsOnTaskID: UUID!, type: DependencyType): TaskDependency!
}
